# Generated by Cargo
# will have compiled files and executables
debug
target

# These are backup files generated by rustfmt
**/*.rs.bk

# MSVC Windows builds of rustc generate these, which store debugging information
*.pdb

# Generated by cargo mutants
# Contains mutation testing data
**/mutants.out*/

# RustRover
#  JetBrains specific template is maintained in a separate JetBrains.gitignore that can
#  be found at https://github.com/github/gitignore/blob/main/Global/JetBrains.gitignore
#  and can be added to the global gitignore or merged into this file.  For a more nuclear
#  option (not recommended) you can uncomment the following to ignore the entire idea folder.
#.idea/


# Added by cargo

/target


# Added by cargo
#
# already existing elements were commented out

#/target

# Reference specifications and validation artefacts (see spec/README.md).
# Not committed: the CEN validation artefacts are EUPL-1.2 and the vendor
# specifications carry their own terms — keeping them out of the repo keeps
# both crates' MIT OR Apache-2.0 licensing clean. Fetch with `just spec`.
#
# One tree at the workspace root, serving both crates. It used to be two.
/spec/


# Local working notes, kept out of the repository.
#
# Anchored to the root, which matters. These were once bare filenames, and a bare
# pattern matches at *any* depth; on a case-insensitive filesystem, the default
# on macOS, it also matches a different case. One of them collided with a
# documentation page, which was then silently untracked: it existed locally, the
# site built locally, and CI failed on a broken link to a page that had never
# been pushed. `just tracked` now asserts this cannot recur.
#
# `git status` does not list an ignored file, so nothing pointed at the cause.
/NOTES.md
/notes/
# Correspondence drafted for another project's maintainers. Written here because
# this is where the evidence is; not part of this repository's documentation.
/FEEDBACK_*.md
.DS_Store
# Python bytecode from codegen/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Zola's build output for the documentation site (see `just site`).
/site/public/

# Internal architecture notes (see concepts/README.md).
#
# Anchored, for the reason the block above gives. These are working documents:
# they cite the specifications by clause, quote the artefacts, and record what
# each design decision cost — none of which is a claim this repository makes to
# its users. `site/` is the public narrative and `CHANGELOG.md` the history;
# `concepts/` is neither, and is not scanned by `just tracked` because it is not
# a directory the build reads.
/concepts/
